# Golang Services

## Stack (pinned — see docs/tech-stack.md)

- **Go 1.27.x** (`go 1.27` in go.mod)
- Web: **Gin** v1.12.x (not Echo)
- ORM: **GORM** v1.31.x + postgres driver
- Kafka: **segmentio/kafka-go** v0.4.x (not Sarama by default)
- Redis: **go-redis/v9**
- WebSockets: gorilla/websocket (`realtime-service`)
- Tests: testify

## Layout (per service under `backend/go-services/{name}/`)

```
cmd/server/main.go
internal/{handler,service,repository,model,config,kafka}
go.mod
```

## API & config

- REST under `/api/v1/...` matching `docs/services-mvp.md`
- Config via environment variables (DB, Redis, Kafka brokers)
- Health endpoint: `GET /health` or `/api/v1/health`

## Data & events

- Models match tables owned by Go services in `docs/database.md`
- Consumers: idempotent processing
- Producers: only after successful DB write
- Redis: cache, queues, pub/sub (realtime)

## Do

- Thin handlers; logic in `service`; pass `context.Context` on I/O

## Don't

- Mix Echo/Fiber with Gin
- Default to Sarama unless there is a documented reason to switch
